# ADR-0317 (F-27): RESET takes priority over the work queued ahead of it.
# One write carries RUN "UNWIND range(1, 3) AS x RETURN x", PULL {n: -1},
# RESET, RUN "RETURN 2 AS y", PULL {n: -1}: the RUN and PULL ahead of RESET
# answer IGNORED (no RECORDs), RESET answers SUCCESS, the rest run normally.
# An ordinary exchange comes first: a RAW first C: line would turn off the
# automatic handshake and AUTO HELLO.
!: BOLT 4.4
!: AUTO HELLO
!: AUTO GOODBYE

C: RUN "RETURN 1 AS x" {} {}
S: SUCCESS {"fields": ["x"]}
C: PULL {"n": -1}
S: RECORD [1]
   SUCCESS {}

C: <RAW> 00 26 B3 10 D0 20 55 4E 57 49 4E 44 20 72 61 6E 67 65 28 31 2C 20 33 29 20 41 53 20 78 20 52 45 54 55 52 4E 20 78 A0 A0 00 00 00 06 B1 3F A1 81 6E FF 00 00 00 02 B0 0F 00 00 00 12 B3 10 8D 52 45 54 55 52 4E 20 32 20 41 53 20 79 A0 A0 00 00 00 06 B1 3F A1 81 6E FF 00 00
S: IGNORED
   IGNORED
   SUCCESS {}
   SUCCESS {"fields": ["y"]}
   RECORD [2]
   SUCCESS {}
